{"id": "clm:47ce7029c041ba4052e0520f7d931d9134ba72b5846b0fe1e46ba03e417ff119", "type": "statement", "text": "The ESR baseline places equality keys first, sort keys next, and range keys last when preserving index sort order is the priority. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/ten-recommendations-for-running-your-mongodb-environment/", "https://github.com/OneUptime/blog/blob/master/posts/2026-01-30-mongodb-compound-index-strategies/README.md", "https://ozgurgurcan.com/blog/mongodb-compound-indexes-esr-rule", "https://percona.university/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/MongoDB-Performance-issues-Troubleshooting-methods-2.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:581447a248646dd57abeb0f5fbc28cc181dd0f7e5432ea75ac97d5bb88d55915", "type": "statement", "text": "The documented 201-or-more case treats $in as range-like for sorting: subsequent index keys cannot supply the requested sort. Place typically large lists with range fields when designing for ESR. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://dev.to/mongodb/or-expansion-in-mongodb-and-how-in-is-treated-as-a-range-with-skip-scan-or-an-equality-for-2b38"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2d8f4daca17b566616542b256da162181707acf7da8c5656f5b352c7dbe9fd75"]}
{"id": "clm:606f92a66e1bd6e7c2844e95b47f73a80cda1622e978d31e253cbe693e55eb33", "type": "statement", "text": "The 201-element boundary is not guaranteed across versions; the historical SERVER-14034 fix raised the scan-expansion limit from 50 to 200 in MongoDB 2.6.4. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-14034"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2d8f4daca17b566616542b256da162181707acf7da8c5656f5b352c7dbe9fd75", "ev:7fd44f2952fa0e886492215c389f33d868ff0bc2c990246ebd0d9d21558199fe"]}
{"id": "clm:c49555ee3748b3123172078d1f04434656658bc72d3b018eda9344b987a9c35c", "type": "statement", "text": "ERS can outperform ESR when a selective range reduces enough work to justify a blocking sort; ESR is a guideline rather than a universal optimum. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://dev.to/mongodb/or-expansion-in-mongodb-and-how-in-is-treated-as-a-range-with-skip-scan-or-an-equality-for-2b38", "https://ozgurgurcan.com/blog/mongodb-compound-indexes-esr-rule"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bc8c6a9b2cf1b7d8f92a2231b3750a93a424f64c678b9b06562ff44581969dd2", "ev:f91688a1eec442ce3c34eae52ae9eccae12f4a014944029ff4069bdfeb8f8b96"]}
{"id": "clm:b19384998334ee1f4e69e802fc169b99688390c8784a32109468cc33c9a0f406", "type": "statement", "text": "Validate index placement with explain('executionStats') on representative queries and list sizes. Inspect SORT versus SORT_MERGE and compare keys and documents examined instead of assuming that IXSCAN alone proves sort support. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://dev.to/mongodb/or-expansion-in-mongodb-and-how-in-is-treated-as-a-range-with-skip-scan-or-an-equality-for-2b38", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/OneUptime/blog/blob/master/posts/2026-01-30-mongodb-compound-index-strategies/README.md", "https://www.percona.com/blog/ten-recommendations-for-running-your-mongodb-environment/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ada09142808ec2c7cc5edd9f03ba49168c3f1f4d51b66143407419a14563c1e", "ev:4d95f0da1a5d992dde66e74ecf030903cffecf186857fb6dbfb9f1d3a0aa1311"]}
{"id": "clm:5aa3cce11f497ed112c55006a4e03cb6bc5f21f7fcade88c1fe3112091c84816", "type": "statement", "text": "For sort-bearing queries, place typically small $in lists with equality predicates and typically large lists with range predicates; verify the plan rather than treating $in as unconditional equality. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://ozgurgurcan.com/blog/mongodb-compound-indexes-esr-rule"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:44dd28b0749d6d0da109661e21ec88e318e9355996e546b18f41da87f8e3847c", "type": "statement", "text": "Compare candidate index orders using hint() and explain('executionStats'); inspect SORT versus SORT_MERGE and compare keys/documents examined with rows returned. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://ozgurgurcan.com/blog/mongodb-compound-indexes-esr-rule"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:267698607c21c307d258ad3e689004f71a3f5542619ab84ac864d186985dfd17", "ev:4f79c4aff908fd64df93802ab91438397291ef4b3286b82cd7105f83389fb73d"]}
{"id": "clm:0d66841fec55f4ecd85d6e204e624b6abd0f03b8f18c8db4e38ef4bd8a312207", "type": "statement", "text": "Equality keys can appear in any relative order for a query that constrains all of them to exact values. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://ozgurgurcan.com/blog/mongodb-compound-indexes-esr-rule"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:174143d9ceef7fa9dd6f8853d9e4c78590c5990836e5a8397265b0009dda2223", "type": "statement", "text": "For eligible sorted queries, the documented small-list case is fewer than 201 $in elements: ordered index scans can feed SORT_MERGE, making the $in key equality-like before the sort keys. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://dev.to/mongodb/or-expansion-in-mongodb-and-how-in-is-treated-as-a-range-with-skip-scan-or-an-equality-for-2b38"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2d8f4daca17b566616542b256da162181707acf7da8c5656f5b352c7dbe9fd75"]}
{"id": "clm:7edf792cd2d286f29b5dde8b07fdbaef9d62d5a65f415b21d5e93074aa6b2b1a", "type": "statement", "text": "SERVER-14034 documents multiplication across $in prefixes: ten values on a and six on b require 60 scans for sorting c under {a:1,b:1,c:1}. That exceeded the historical 50-scan cap; small individual lists therefore did not guarantee expansion. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-14034", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:765c841a4b611925e6c93dac04a9e4312ce89b6f510c9c942236da0895204629"]}
{"id": "clm:80f6fb698b091501afa6aa05587ebf65eed8b100a365e2ed6474d25ccc3046ef", "type": "statement", "text": "$in alone performs equality matches; with sorting, short lists can be expanded and combined through SORT_MERGE, while long lists behave like ranges for index ordering. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://ozgurgurcan.com/blog/mongodb-compound-indexes-esr-rule"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:6dcbda92ef3d2a48108cbf1ffb56f4ef5260ad0b0e731710cf0a3f008cb2e3d3", "type": "statement", "text": "The MongoDB guide documents fewer than 201 $in elements as expandable with sort, and 201 or more as range-like, preventing subsequent index fields from supplying sort. It explicitly warns this cutoff can vary across versions. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/equality-sort-range-guideline.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["ESR guideline and $in placement in compound indexes"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c3333af3b54b8af6d975621e5cb0777699d74a77cfbe86956f0492fcf0bb0c7f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2d8f4daca17b566616542b256da162181707acf7da8c5656f5b352c7dbe9fd75"]}
